---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

import ContactCTA from "../components/ContactCTA.astro";
import Hero from "../components/Hero.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="About | Michael Miller" description="About Michael Miller">
  <div class="stack gap-20">
    <main class="wrapper about">
      <Hero
        kicker="The longer version"
        title="Builder with a project-manager's brain."
        tagline="Construction taught me how to sequence work. Software is how I ship it."
      >
        <img
          width="1553"
          height="873"
          src="/assets/profilephoto_two.jpg"
          alt="Michael volunteering at a local event in his community."
        />
      </Hero>

      <section data-reveal>
        <h2 class="section-title">Background</h2>
        <div class="content">
          <p>
            I'm a full-stack software developer at Pingram, a developer
            messaging platform for email, SMS, and inbound communication. Day
            to day that means the React dashboard, AWS Lambda APIs, generated
            SDKs, CLI, docs, and the pipelines that ship them.
          </p>
          <p>
            Before Pingram I built web and mobile products at Get Coding, after
            completing their full-stack program. That career started in
            construction and project management — planning, sequencing work, and
            getting teams across the finish line — which still shows up in how I
            break down software work.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="timeline-section" data-reveal>
        <h2 class="section-title">Experience</h2>
        <ol class="timeline">
          <li>
            <p class="when">2024 – present</p>
            <div>
              <h3>Pingram <span>(formerly NotificationAPI)</span></h3>
              <p class="role">Full Stack Software Developer</p>
              <p>
                Product engineering across the dashboard, serverless backend, SDKs,
                CLI, GitHub Actions integrations, and documentation. Most of the
                work is TypeScript on AWS: Lambda, API Gateway, DynamoDB, SES, and
                the surrounding observability and CI.
              </p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <p class="when">2023 – 2024</p>
            <div>
              <h3>Get Coding Training Inc.</h3>
              <p class="role">Full Stack and Mobile Application Developer</p>
              <p>
                Built and maintained the student/coach tracking product across web
                and React Native, including student-facing mobile features and a
                recruitment dashboard for partner companies.
              </p>
            </div>
          </li>
        </ol>
      </section>

      <section data-reveal>
        <h2 class="section-title">Education</h2>
        <div class="content">
          <p class="role">Get Coding · Full Stack Development</p>
          <p>Jan 2022 – March 2023</p>
          <p>
            After a few years wanting to move into tech, I joined
            <a href="https://getcoding.ca" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Get Coding</a>
            and trained weekly with working software developers in React, Node.js,
            PostgreSQL, and AWS.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section data-reveal>
        <h2 class="section-title">Skills</h2>
        <div class="content">
          <p>
            TypeScript and React for product UI; Node.js and AWS Lambda for
            APIs; DynamoDB, SES, SNS, and SQS for data and delivery; CDK and
            Serverless Framework for infrastructure. I also spend a lot of time
            on developer-facing work: OpenAPI-generated SDKs, CLI packaging,
            docs in Astro, and CI with GitHub Actions. Earlier work includes
            React Native, PostgreSQL, and GraphQL/AppSync.
          </p>
          <ul class="chips">
            <li>TypeScript</li>
            <li>React</li>
            <li>AWS Lambda</li>
            <li>DynamoDB</li>
            <li>CDK</li>
            <li>OpenAPI</li>
            <li>GitHub Actions</li>
            <li>Astro</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    <ContactCTA />
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 3.5rem;
  }

  img {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    width: 100%;
    max-height: 28rem;
    object-fit: cover;
    object-position: center 20%;
    border-radius: 1.6rem;
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-lg);
    border: 1px solid var(--glass-border);
  }

  section {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--gray-200);
  }

  .section-title {
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
    color: var(--gray-0);
  }

  .content {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.85rem;
  }

  .content :global(a) {
    text-decoration: 1px solid underline transparent;
    text-underline-offset: 0.25em;
    transition: text-decoration-color var(--theme-transition);
  }

  .content :global(a:hover),
  .content :global(a:focus) {
    text-decoration-color: currentColor;
  }

  .timeline {
    list-style: none;
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .timeline li {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.35rem;
    padding: 1.25rem 1.2rem;
    border-radius: 1.2rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--glass-border);
    background: var(--surface);
  }

  .when {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent-bright);
  }

  .timeline h3 {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
  }

  .timeline h3 span {
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--gray-400);
    font-size: 0.85em;
  }

  .role {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--gray-100);
  }

  .chips {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.45rem;
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0.4rem 0 0;
  }

  .chips li {
    padding: 0.35rem 0.75rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    border: 1px solid var(--glass-border);
    background: var(--surface);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
  }

  @media (min-width: 50em) {
    .about {
      max-width: 52rem;
      margin-inline: auto;
    }

    .timeline li {
      grid-template-columns: 9.5rem 1fr;
      gap: 1.5rem;
      padding: 1.5rem 1.6rem;
    }
  }
</style>
